This is where pancake stands: what runs today, where the edges are, and where the
project is going. The code is the truth about the present. The documents linked
below argue the direction without ever pretending unfinished work has already
landed.

## What ships today

[What ships today](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/docs/shipped.md)
is the gated inventory of implemented behavior: the wire operation surface, both
codecs, three netlayers, the actor layer, third-party handoffs, and live
[Goblins](https://spritely.institute/goblins/) interop from every binding. Each claim there is held by a gate, a scenario, or a
live interop run, and a claim that stops matching the tree is treated as a bug.

## Where the edges are

[The boundaries](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/docs/boundaries.md)
name where the implemented surface ends, plainly: transport is cleartext TCP with
encryption riding the separate iroh artifact, bootstrap registrations live for the
process, the OCapN Null fails closed, and the `griddle` network simulator is not
built yet. Reading the edges is the surest way to know what you can rely on.

## Where it is going

Three documents carry the direction. The
[vision](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/docs/vision.md) is the
goal: to be the most performant OCapN implementation there is, fully canonical
and proven by interop, with that performance held to a measured contract rather than
asserted. The
[ladder](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/docs/ladder.md) is the
ordered route to 1.0 with each rung's standing, and the
[roadmap](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/docs/roadmap.md) is the
concrete remaining work.

## Why the boundaries sit where they do

The [decision records](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/docs/decisions/README.md)
are the accepted ADRs: the netlayer contract, the one-parser framing, the C ABI
allocation context, the iroh sidecar, and the rest. When a boundary moves, a
superseding record explains the move rather than leaving the old reasoning to
mislead.
